  "body": "MAINLINE-043 complete, QUESTIONABLE / PROJECTION. Actual frame and lifetime Pf remain null: none of the retrieved grades supplies matched full-member compression statistics. SA is the closest catalogue compression comparison, not a qualified reliability winner.\n\nThe selected target has 1.19810 GPa peak compression including L/1000 bow, or 1.26913 GPa with the explicit joint-moment proxy. Longitudinal tension is zero in those ideal fields; contact, hoop and other principal stresses remain unresolved. Frozen 026b recovery covers 1,680 members. Owner rise-8 forces remain independently unverified.\n\nFor 433-member risk bookkeeping and hypothetical compression m=10, whole-member characteristic strengths of 4.38651/8.75267 GPa meet tube-only frame targets 1e-3/1e-6. These are 1.12475/2.24427 times an assumed 3.9 GPa scale; the catalogue value is not that calibrated scale. Holding that scale instead requires m=10.996/16.849. Reference-volume and tensile-flaw sensitivities are explicit. Actual improvement factor is unknown.\n\nThe needed property is confidence-qualified finished-member lower-tail strength under actual combined stress. Proof qualification would require full-part and joint coverage; an illustrative 1.37428 MN proof exceeds the source stability multiplier. Cost class is high/custom qualification with recurring 100% inspection, not a quote.\n\nTwenty-six input pins, 17 evidence rows, 210 scientific checks and 78 packaging checks are recorded. Four admitted postprocessing jobs released; 16 open NFIs are nonblocking. Brief names no successor: stop/file and SLEEPING.",
